{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1486140-new-abyssal-the-hidden-face","id":1486140,"title":"[New Abyssal] The Hidden Face","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-09T21:45:41-07:00","id":1486140,"title":"[New Abyssal] The Hidden Face","content":"It is shaped like a person. It is pale, emaciated and hairless.<br /> <br /> It trembles and holds itself as if feeling cold or afraid.<br /> <br /> It has its back turned to you, and is staring at a wall.<br /> <br /> Something always prevents you from looking at its face.<br /> <br /> The only way to reveal the truth is to get very close to it.<br /> <br /> Bring a handheld mirror.<br /> <br /> You must turn your back to the entity.<br /> <br /> Remain silent and still.<br /> <br /> You will feel a hand on your shoulder.<br /> <br /> Look into the mirror and don't scream.<br /> <br /> Now the entity knows your face too.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Game Mechanics:</b></u><br /> <br /> The Hidden Face has no stats of its own. It appears at random, and probably as a function of another Abyssal Resonance. One does not have to directly invoke this entity, and in fact, it cannot be done. It is essentially a test of one's curiosity. If the Mage refuses to investigate the Hidden Face at all, his next Paradox roll scores +1 Success, but otherwise the entity leaves them alone. If they do investigate, the entity turns from them, and ultimately ends up fleeing/disappearing in one way or another.<br /> <br /> This is treated as a Mystery with a default Opacity of (Wisdom), or (Wisdom/2 Rounded Up) if the Mage has access to an Advanced Library about the Abyss. As the Mage progresses, they corner the entity in different places, get physically closer, catch brief and partial glimpses, and so forth. This gives the usual rewards of Arcane Beats and Mana, as per Obsessions or equivalent. Deep Revelation consists of finding a way to observe-without-sight, usually through a specific type of reflective surface. The Mage must willingly and knowingly invite the Hidden Face to look at him.<br /> <br /> The Mage will see the Hidden Face on the other side of an Abyssal Iris contained within the tool of indirect visualization, and the entity will be smiling as if inviting him to have a deeper conversation. If the Mage accepts, the Hidden Face becomes that of the Old Man, the Aeon of the Abyss. The Old Man proposes a philosophical question: does the Mage care more about being right or being true? Regardless of how the Mage answers, choosing to engage with the Abyss like this is an Act Of Falling Hubris. The Old Man will continue to test the curiosity of the Mage with additional conversations in future Chapters, and for each such conversation that the Mage seriously attempts to engage with, it counts as another Act Of Falling Hubris.<br /> <br /> The Mage can request that the Old Man go away at any time, since the latter is not interested in tempting the Mage as such, but in showing him the folly of embracing the Abyss. As a side-effect of such exposure, every dot of Wisdom that the Mage loses will give him 2 Arcane XP to spend on Abyssal versions of traits such as Artifacts, Rotes, Praxes, Grimoires, Familiars and more. This is in addition to the 1 Arcane Beat gained from risking the Act Of Falling Hubris. If the Mage suffers a Dramatic Failure on any of these Acts Of Falling Hubris, the ST can inflict a Persistent Hubris Condition related to the Abyss. The Old Man will notice this and offer guidance on how to Resolve it, but in such a way that might be misinterpreted by the Mage as an invitation to delve even further into the Abyss. At this point, initiation into a Scelestus Legacy and worse things still cannot be too far away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 11-09-2022, 08:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}